		<!-- Content -->
		<div class="container">
			<h1 class="mt-4">How to Add a Film</h1>

            <h2 class="mt-4">Overview</h2>
			<p>
				Film Tracker allows you to add films or series to your personal collection
				and keep track of the movies and shows you have watched. With that you can easily 
                manage rankings, reviews, and other information about your watched content.
				
			</p>

            <h2>How to use this feature</h2>

			<h3 class="mt-4">1. Open the Add Film Modal</h3>

			<p>
				To add a new film, click the button used to add a film in the application.
				A modal window will appear, allowing you to enter the information about the film.
			</p>

			<p>
				Fill in the required fields with the movie's information.
				Once you have entered the details, confirm the action to add the film to your collection.
			</p>

			<img
				src="/images/add-film-modal.png"
				alt="Add Film modal showing the fields used to enter movie information"
				class="img-fluid rounded border mb-3"
			>

			<h3 class="mt-4">2. View Your Film Collection</h3>

			<p>
				After adding the film or the series, it will appear in your collection on the main interface.
				You can repeat this process to add more films and build your personal collection.
			</p>

			<img
				src="/images/films-added.png"
				alt="Film Tracker interface displaying a collection of added films"
				class="img-fluid rounded border mb-3"
			>

			<h3 class="mt-4">Tips</h3>

			<ul>
				<li>Make sure to fill in all required fields before confirming.<br>
                    Like the title, rank & if it's a film or series.
                </li>
				<li>Check the movie information before adding it to your collection.</li>
				<li>You can repeat the process whenever you want to add another film or series  .</li>
			</ul>

			<p class="mt-4 mb-4">
				<a href="/documentation">Back to Documentation</a>
			</p>
		</div>

